      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Toronto Maple Leafs aren't mourning a season that ended with 78 points and an 8th-place finish in the Atlantic; they're building a new one. <strong>The club has parted ways with assistant general manager Hayley Wickenheiser</strong>, a move that signals a shifting front-office philosophy as free agency opens. With the roster frozen since April, attention now turns to Ben Danford, the Marlies standout who's setting his sights on an opening-night spot in Toronto. Cap flexibility is tight, but the draft and free-agent market offer a chance to inject youth and depth without breaking the bank. The Leafs need a true two-way center and a reliable bottom-six winger more than anything. <strong>What to watch in the next week: whether Danford earns a contract and if the Leafs aggressively pursue a veteran forward to balance the lineup</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated July 11, 2026"
      },
