        "body": "The summer heat in Las Vegas isn't just from the sun; it's from the <strong>Raptors' rookie Allen Graves exploding for 22 points and 13 rebounds in his Summer League debut</strong>, a performance that may already rank as the best opening night in franchise history. Graves, the team's latest pick, didn't just show up - he dominated, forcing Mark Davis and the front office to ask whether this kid is the missing piece after a 46-36 season that ended 69 days ago in the Atlantic Division's third spot. Scottie Barnes, trying to mold the next wave, told reporters Kawhi Leonard's old crew needs the kids to \"learn fast\" after a narrow 83-80 Summer League loss to the Celtics. The real story isn't the loss; it's the emergence. <strong>What Graves does in the next two Vegas games will define whether the Raptors' draft gamble finally pays off.</strong>",
